--TEST--
`Core\Random\Seeded::bytes` returns `tainted bytes` and `::token` returns `tainted string`, and every key parameter refuses a `tainted` argument, so a key anyone can predict from its seed does not compile into a seal, a signature, a token or a code — `rule:security/secret-has-no-ambient-source`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A seeded generator gives the same bytes for the same seed. Anyone who knows the
// seed can make them again, so none of these calls compiles.
Core\Random\Seeded $generator = new Core\Random\Seeded(42);
bytes $key = $generator->bytes(32);
Core\Crypto::seal('message' as bytes, $generator->bytes(32), Core\Crypto::Cipher::XChaCha20Poly1305);
Core\SignedCookie::seal('uid', '7', [$generator->bytes(32)]);
Core\Csrf::issue('session', $generator->bytes(32));
Core\Hash::hmac('payload', $generator->bytes(32), Core\Hash::Digest::Sha256);
Core\Totp::code($generator->bytes(20));
string $token = $generator->token();

// A key from `Core\Crypto::generateKey` is not predictable, so this call compiles.
Core\Crypto::seal('message' as bytes, Core\Crypto::generateKey(), Core\Crypto::Cipher::XChaCha20Poly1305);
--EXPECT--

